lib/IO/K8s/AutoGen.pm POD describes get_or_generate as the entry point
but names none of the ways it refuses.

After karr #55/#56 the list is longer and one entry is new:

- unresolved $ref in a property, in items, or in additionalProperties
  --> croaks (karr #56). NEW: a partial spec referencing definitions it
  does not ship used to generate the class successfully, minus those
  fields, losing their data on every round-trip.
- additionalProperties that is neither a schema object nor a boolean
  --> croaks naming class and field (karr #55)
- the pre-existing GVK croaks in _select_gvk_entry

A caller passing an openapi_spec needs to know get_or_generate can die,
and on what. Worth stating the one partial-spec case that still works:
a top-level CRD schema whose metadata $refs the standard ObjectMeta
without shipping its definition -- metadata is skipped before the ref is
looked at (karr #60).

Also note the observable side effect of that skip: when all_defs does
carry ObjectMeta and nothing else references it, it no longer appears in
IO::K8s::AutoGen::generated_classes().

Found by the autogen lane while implementing karr #55-#57/#60.
